steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1793593060
      nanos: 518451296
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
    source_trajectory_step_info {
      trajectory_id: "8b87e245-6f73-4c1d-ac0b-810fe8bc2268"
      step_index: 1
      cascade_id: "8b87e245-6f73-4c1d-ac0b-810fe8bc2268"
    }
    model_api_content_id: "c4e2054540994097b58b9542493f0bbc"
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# Build StockSense \342\200\224 A Modern Stock Research & News Platform\n\nAct as a senior full-stack developer, product designer, and financial technology UX specialist.\n\nBuild a complete, functional, responsive web application named **StockSense**.\n\n## 1. Product Vision\n\nStockSense is intended to become an all-in-one stock research and paper-trading platform where users can understand financial markets, research companies, track stocks, and eventually practice trading.\n\nFor this initial MVP, focus ONLY on the **Stock News module**.\n\nDo not implement paper trading, real trading, AI trading agents, brokerage integrations, portfolio management, or order execution yet. Keep the architecture modular so these features can be added later.\n\nThe current product should feel like a real financial research terminal, not a generic news blog or landing page.\n\n## 2. Technology Stack\n\nUse:\n- React with TypeScript\n- Vite\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Lucide React icons\n- Recharts for charts if needed\n- Node.js server-side API routes for secure external API integration\n- A reliable financial news API or reputable news source integration\n\nUse clean, modular, maintainable code.\n\nDo not expose API keys in frontend code. Store secrets in server-side environment variables.\n\n## 3. Brand Identity & Visual Design\n\nBrand name: StockSense\n\nTagline: \"Understand the Market. Make Smarter Decisions.\"\n\nDesign direction:\n- Premium financial terminal aesthetic\n- Dark-first interface\n- Professional, clean, minimal, data-dense but easy to read\n- Inspired by modern financial research platforms such as Bloomberg, TradingView, and premium fintech dashboards, without copying their interfaces\n- Background: deep navy/charcoal (#0B0F14)\n- Cards: slightly lighter charcoal (#121821)\n- Accent: electric blue (#3B82F6)\n- Positive movement: muted green\n- Negative movement: muted red\n- Typography: Inter or a similar modern sans-serif\n- Use subtle borders, restrained shadows, smooth hover states, and consistent spacing\n- Avoid excessive gradients, glassmorphism, giant rounded cards, and unnecessary animations\n\nThe design must look credible to investors, traders, and students researching the stock market.\n\n## 4. Application Layout\n\nCreate a full dashboard interface with:\n\n### A. Sidebar Navigation\n- StockSense logo and wordmark\n- Market Overview\n- Stock News (active)\n- Company Research (Coming Soon)\n- Watchlist (Coming Soon)\n- Paper Trading (Coming Soon)\n- Settings\n\nOnly Stock News should be functional in this MVP.\n\nComing Soon pages should be clearly marked and must not pretend to have working functionality.\n\nSidebar should be collapsible on desktop and convert into a mobile navigation drawer.\n\n### B. Top Navigation Bar\n- Global search input: \"Search stocks, companies, or news...\"\n- Market status indicator\n- Current date\n- Refresh news button\n- User profile/avatar placeholder\n\nSearch should support searching article headlines, companies, and stock tickers within the available news dataset.\n\n### C. Market Ticker Strip\nDisplay a horizontally scrollable market ticker showing:\n- NIFTY 50\n- SENSEX\n- BANK NIFTY\n- S&P 500\n- NASDAQ Composite\n- Dow Jones\n\nEach item should show:\n- Index name\n- Latest value\n- Absolute change\n- Percentage change\n- Green/red movement indicator\n\nUse a reliable market-data API if configured.\n\nIf live market data is unavailable, clearly label values as demo data. Never present fabricated prices as real-time data.\n\n## 5. Stock News Dashboard\n\nThis is the primary page and the most important part of the application.\n\n### Page Header\nTitle: \"Stock News\"\n\nSubtitle: \"Stay informed about the stories moving the markets.\"\n\nShow:\n- Last updated timestamp\n- Refresh button\n- News count\n\n### News Category Filters\n\nCreate functional filter tabs:\n- All News\n- Indian Markets\n- Global Markets\n- Stocks & Companies\n- Economy\n- Earnings\n- IPOs\n- Commodities\n- Technology\n\nAdd additional filter controls:\n- Market: India / US / Global\n- Time: Latest / Today / This Week\n- Sort: Most Recent / Relevance\n\nFilters must actually update the displayed articles.\n\n### Featured News Section\n\nCreate a visually prominent featured article section with:\n- Headline\n- Short summary\n- Publisher\n- Published time\n- Relevant image\n- Market/category label\n- \"Read Full Story\" link\n\nUse the most relevant recent article from the fetched news data.\n\n### News Feed\n\nCreate a professional news feed with article cards or compact rows.\n\nEach article should display:\n- Headline\n- Short summary or description\n- Publisher/source\n- Published date and relative time\n- Thumbnail image when available\n- Related company names and stock tickers\n- News category\n- Market tag\n- External article link\n\nMake headlines the visual focus.\n\nUse a compact, readable layout suitable for users reading many articles.\n\nAdd:\n- Load more / pagination\n- Empty state\n- Loading skeletons\n- Error state with retry\n- Responsive layout\n\nDo not duplicate articles. Deduplicate using article URL and normalized headline.\n\n### Trending News\n\nAdd a right-side panel on desktop containing:\n- Trending stories\n- Most mentioned companies\n- Popular market topics\n\nOn mobile, move this section below the news feed.\n\nTrending companies should be derived from actual article mentions when possible. Do not fabricate popularity rankings.\n\n## 6. Article Details\n\nWhen a user clicks a news article, open a dedicated article detail page or side panel.\n\nShow:\n- Full headline\n- Publisher and source link\n- Published date and time\n- Article image\n- Full available description\n- Related tickers and companies\n- Category\n- Original article link\n\nInclude a button: \"Read Original Article\"\n\nOpen the publisher\'s original article in a new tab.\n\nDo not scrape or reproduce copyrighted full articles. Display only the headline, metadata, and short summaries permitted by the source.\n\n## 7. News Data Integration\n\nImplement real news fetching wherever possible.\n\nPreferred sources:\n- NewsAPI\n- Finnhub company news\n- Alpha Vantage news and sentiment\n- Other reputable financial news APIs with suitable coverage and licensing\n\nPrioritize coverage of Indian equities and global markets.\n\nUse a backend service layer with a unified article data model.\n\nExample fields:\n- id\n- title\n- summary\n- source\n- url\n- imageUrl\n- publishedAt\n- category\n- market\n- relatedTickers\n- sentiment, only if provided by a reliable source\n\nCreate a provider abstraction so news APIs can be changed without rewriting the UI.\n\nUse environment variables for API keys.\n\nIf no API key is configured:\n- Render a polished demo experience using clearly labeled sample articles\n- Show a visible \"Demo News\" indicator\n- Never claim sample articles are breaking or live news\n- Provide clear instructions for connecting a real news API\n\nImplement:\n- Loading states\n- API error handling\n- Request timeouts\n- Rate-limit handling\n- Refresh functionality\n- Caching where appropriate\n- Fallback behavior\n\nDo not use fabricated timestamps or claim live updates when the source is not live.\n\n## 8. User Experience\n\nMake the interface feel fast and intuitive.\n\nInclude:\n- Functional search\n- Working category filters\n- Working market and time filters\n- Sorting\n- Refresh button\n- Article detail navigation\n- External source links\n- Responsive sidebar\n- Smooth but restrained transitions\n- Keyboard-accessible controls\n- Clear hover and focus states\n\nPersist user interface preferences such as selected theme and filters locally if appropriate.\n\nDo not add authentication in this MVP.\n\n## 9. Future-Ready Architecture\n\nKeep the code organized into reusable components:\n\n- Sidebar\n- Topbar\n- MarketTicker\n- NewsDashboard\n- FeaturedNews\n- NewsFeed\n- NewsCard\n- NewsFilters\n- TrendingPanel\n- ArticleDetail\n- NewsService\n- MarketDataService\n\nSeparate frontend components, API routes, data models, and service logic.\n\nDo not implement future trading features. Only prepare a clean architecture that allows future modules to be added without rebuilding the news system.\n\n## 10. Quality Requirements\n\n- Build a complete working application, not just a static design.\n- Do not leave buttons nonfunctional.\n- Do not use placeholder links such as \"#\".\n- Do not invent financial data or news.\n- Avoid unnecessary components and excessive visual clutter.\n- Ensure TypeScript types are correct.\n- Ensure the app runs without compilation errors.\n- Test the app in the preview and fix runtime issues.\n- Make the desktop experience excellent while ensuring full mobile responsiveness.\n\n## Final Deliverable\n\nGenerate the complete StockSense web application with the Stock News dashboard as the default route.\n\nThe first impression should be that StockSense is a serious, premium financial research product with a strong foundation for future expansion.\n\nPrioritize visual quality, real news integration, usability, and clean architecture."
    items {
      text: "# Build StockSense \342\200\224 A Modern Stock Research & News Platform\n\nAct as a senior full-stack developer, product designer, and financial technology UX specialist.\n\nBuild a complete, functional, responsive web application named **StockSense**.\n\n## 1. Product Vision\n\nStockSense is intended to become an all-in-one stock research and paper-trading platform where users can understand financial markets, research companies, track stocks, and eventually practice trading.\n\nFor this initial MVP, focus ONLY on the **Stock News module**.\n\nDo not implement paper trading, real trading, AI trading agents, brokerage integrations, portfolio management, or order execution yet. Keep the architecture modular so these features can be added later.\n\nThe current product should feel like a real financial research terminal, not a generic news blog or landing page.\n\n## 2. Technology Stack\n\nUse:\n- React with TypeScript\n- Vite\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Lucide React icons\n- Recharts for charts if needed\n- Node.js server-side API routes for secure external API integration\n- A reliable financial news API or reputable news source integration\n\nUse clean, modular, maintainable code.\n\nDo not expose API keys in frontend code. Store secrets in server-side environment variables.\n\n## 3. Brand Identity & Visual Design\n\nBrand name: StockSense\n\nTagline: \"Understand the Market. Make Smarter Decisions.\"\n\nDesign direction:\n- Premium financial terminal aesthetic\n- Dark-first interface\n- Professional, clean, minimal, data-dense but easy to read\n- Inspired by modern financial research platforms such as Bloomberg, TradingView, and premium fintech dashboards, without copying their interfaces\n- Background: deep navy/charcoal (#0B0F14)\n- Cards: slightly lighter charcoal (#121821)\n- Accent: electric blue (#3B82F6)\n- Positive movement: muted green\n- Negative movement: muted red\n- Typography: Inter or a similar modern sans-serif\n- Use subtle borders, restrained shadows, smooth hover states, and consistent spacing\n- Avoid excessive gradients, glassmorphism, giant rounded cards, and unnecessary animations\n\nThe design must look credible to investors, traders, and students researching the stock market.\n\n## 4. Application Layout\n\nCreate a full dashboard interface with:\n\n### A. Sidebar Navigation\n- StockSense logo and wordmark\n- Market Overview\n- Stock News (active)\n- Company Research (Coming Soon)\n- Watchlist (Coming Soon)\n- Paper Trading (Coming Soon)\n- Settings\n\nOnly Stock News should be functional in this MVP.\n\nComing Soon pages should be clearly marked and must not pretend to have working functionality.\n\nSidebar should be collapsible on desktop and convert into a mobile navigation drawer.\n\n### B. Top Navigation Bar\n- Global search input: \"Search stocks, companies, or news...\"\n- Market status indicator\n- Current date\n- Refresh news button\n- User profile/avatar placeholder\n\nSearch should support searching article headlines, companies, and stock tickers within the available news dataset.\n\n### C. Market Ticker Strip\nDisplay a horizontally scrollable market ticker showing:\n- NIFTY 50\n- SENSEX\n- BANK NIFTY\n- S&P 500\n- NASDAQ Composite\n- Dow Jones\n\nEach item should show:\n- Index name\n- Latest value\n- Absolute change\n- Percentage change\n- Green/red movement indicator\n\nUse a reliable market-data API if configured.\n\nIf live market data is unavailable, clearly label values as demo data. Never present fabricated prices as real-time data.\n\n## 5. Stock News Dashboard\n\nThis is the primary page and the most important part of the application.\n\n### Page Header\nTitle: \"Stock News\"\n\nSubtitle: \"Stay informed about the stories moving the markets.\"\n\nShow:\n- Last updated timestamp\n- Refresh button\n- News count\n\n### News Category Filters\n\nCreate functional filter tabs:\n- All News\n- Indian Markets\n- Global Markets\n- Stocks & Companies\n- Economy\n- Earnings\n- IPOs\n- Commodities\n- Technology\n\nAdd additional filter controls:\n- Market: India / US / Global\n- Time: Latest / Today / This Week\n- Sort: Most Recent / Relevance\n\nFilters must actually update the displayed articles.\n\n### Featured News Section\n\nCreate a visually prominent featured article section with:\n- Headline\n- Short summary\n- Publisher\n- Published time\n- Relevant image\n- Market/category label\n- \"Read Full Story\" link\n\nUse the most relevant recent article from the fetched news data.\n\n### News Feed\n\nCreate a professional news feed with article cards or compact rows.\n\nEach article should display:\n- Headline\n- Short summary or description\n- Publisher/source\n- Published date and relative time\n- Thumbnail image when available\n- Related company names and stock tickers\n- News category\n- Market tag\n- External article link\n\nMake headlines the visual focus.\n\nUse a compact, readable layout suitable for users reading many articles.\n\nAdd:\n- Load more / pagination\n- Empty state\n- Loading skeletons\n- Error state with retry\n- Responsive layout\n\nDo not duplicate articles. Deduplicate using article URL and normalized headline.\n\n### Trending News\n\nAdd a right-side panel on desktop containing:\n- Trending stories\n- Most mentioned companies\n- Popular market topics\n\nOn mobile, move this section below the news feed.\n\nTrending companies should be derived from actual article mentions when possible. Do not fabricate popularity rankings.\n\n## 6. Article Details\n\nWhen a user clicks a news article, open a dedicated article detail page or side panel.\n\nShow:\n- Full headline\n- Publisher and source link\n- Published date and time\n- Article image\n- Full available description\n- Related tickers and companies\n- Category\n- Original article link\n\nInclude a button: \"Read Original Article\"\n\nOpen the publisher\'s original article in a new tab.\n\nDo not scrape or reproduce copyrighted full articles. Display only the headline, metadata, and short summaries permitted by the source.\n\n## 7. News Data Integration\n\nImplement real news fetching wherever possible.\n\nPreferred sources:\n- NewsAPI\n- Finnhub company news\n- Alpha Vantage news and sentiment\n- Other reputable financial news APIs with suitable coverage and licensing\n\nPrioritize coverage of Indian equities and global markets.\n\nUse a backend service layer with a unified article data model.\n\nExample fields:\n- id\n- title\n- summary\n- source\n- url\n- imageUrl\n- publishedAt\n- category\n- market\n- relatedTickers\n- sentiment, only if provided by a reliable source\n\nCreate a provider abstraction so news APIs can be changed without rewriting the UI.\n\nUse environment variables for API keys.\n\nIf no API key is configured:\n- Render a polished demo experience using clearly labeled sample articles\n- Show a visible \"Demo News\" indicator\n- Never claim sample articles are breaking or live news\n- Provide clear instructions for connecting a real news API\n\nImplement:\n- Loading states\n- API error handling\n- Request timeouts\n- Rate-limit handling\n- Refresh functionality\n- Caching where appropriate\n- Fallback behavior\n\nDo not use fabricated timestamps or claim live updates when the source is not live.\n\n## 8. User Experience\n\nMake the interface feel fast and intuitive.\n\nInclude:\n- Functional search\n- Working category filters\n- Working market and time filters\n- Sorting\n- Refresh button\n- Article detail navigation\n- External source links\n- Responsive sidebar\n- Smooth but restrained transitions\n- Keyboard-accessible controls\n- Clear hover and focus states\n\nPersist user interface preferences such as selected theme and filters locally if appropriate.\n\nDo not add authentication in this MVP.\n\n## 9. Future-Ready Architecture\n\nKeep the code organized into reusable components:\n\n- Sidebar\n- Topbar\n- MarketTicker\n- NewsDashboard\n- FeaturedNews\n- NewsFeed\n- NewsCard\n- NewsFilters\n- TrendingPanel\n- ArticleDetail\n- NewsService\n- MarketDataService\n\nSeparate frontend components, API routes, data models, and service logic.\n\nDo not implement future trading features. Only prepare a clean architecture that allows future modules to be added without rebuilding the news system.\n\n## 10. Quality Requirements\n\n- Build a complete working application, not just a static design.\n- Do not leave buttons nonfunctional.\n- Do not use placeholder links such as \"#\".\n- Do not invent financial data or news.\n- Avoid unnecessary components and excessive visual clutter.\n- Ensure TypeScript types are correct.\n- Ensure the app runs without compilation errors.\n- Test the app in the preview and fix runtime issues.\n- Make the desktop experience excellent while ensuring full mobile responsiveness.\n\n## Final Deliverable\n\nGenerate the complete StockSense web application with the Stock News dashboard as the default route.\n\nThe first impression should be that StockSense is a serious, premium financial research product with a strong foundation for future expansion.\n\nPrioritize visual quality, real news integration, usability, and clean architecture."
