  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on defining the precise scope. I see the main task is constructing Node.js API routes for secure external API integration. It\'s imperative that I integrate a reliable financial news source, prioritizing Indian equities and the global markets, while keeping API keys secure.\n\n\n**Refining Technical Specifications**\n\nI\'m now detailing front-end needs, considering a demo experience with sample articles if no API key is set, clearly labeling them as such. I\'m also preparing for loading states, error handling, timeouts, and rate limits, along with refresh and caching features. The architectural framework will include `server.ts` and Express. I also need to assess whether we need `recharts` for charts.\n\n\n**Evaluating API Support**\n\nI\'m now investigating API options. I\'m considering Finnhub, NewsAPI, and Alpha Vantage, along with public RSS feeds for news, which may be more flexible. RSS feeds could be valuable, as they provide real-time news without needing an API key. I must figure out how to parse them securely server-side, for optimal reliability.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
