  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Frontend Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the client-side frontend component design, as you requested. I\'ve begun to break down the modular architecture as described. The immediate focus is on the sidebar navigation, its components, and their hierarchy. I will structure it to accommodate the StockSense logo, and the listed features, including the currently active \"Stock News\" module.\n\n\n**Defining New Components**\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing additional frontend elements. My attention is now on the top navigation bar, which will feature a global search, market status, current date, a refresh button, and user profile placeholder. I\'m also planning the market ticker strip, including key indices, their values, and change indicators, clearly marked as demo data. Finally, I\'m working on the design for the \"Stock News\" dashboard page header, including title, subtitle, timestamp, and a refresh button.\n\n\n**Detailing News Feed Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the news feed component, with a focus on its structure and interactive elements. I\'ve broken it into a featured news section and a professional news feed, both of which require interactive elements. The featured section requires visual hierarchy, and the feed needs filters, load-more controls, empty-state messaging, related ticker links, and news category tags. I also have to account for demo data indicators.\n\n\n**Elaborating Feed Interaction**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user interaction elements of the news feed. I\'ve considered zero-match scenarios, including a reset filters button. I am also working on loading skeletons, an error state with retry, and deduplication. I am planning trending news content, too. This right-side panel will show trending stories, mentioned companies (filterable by ticker), and market topics (also filterable).\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_103550"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"import { MarketIndex, NewsApiResponse } from \'../types\';\\n\\nexport async function getNews(forceRefresh = false): Promise<NewsApiResponse> {\\n  const url = forceRefresh ? \'/api/news?refresh=true\' : \'/api/news\';\\n  const res = await fetch(url);\\n  if (!res.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch news: ${res.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return res.json();\\n}\\n\\nexport async function getMarketIndices(): Promise<{ indices: MarketIndex[]; isDemoData: boolean; lastUpdated: string }> {\\n  const res = await fetch(\'/api/market-indices\');\\n  if (!res.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch market indices: ${res.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return res.json();\\n}\\n\\nexport async function getApiStatus(): Promise<{\\n  status: string;\\n  configuredProviders: { finnhub: boolean; newsApi: boolean; alphaVantage: boolean };\\n  usingDemoData: boolean;\\n}> {\\n  const res = await fetch(\'/api/status\');\\n  if (!res.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch API status: ${res.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return res.json();\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Client API service layer for communicating with /api endpoints\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/services/api.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing client API service\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create API service client\"}"
